==Trivia==
*The word "''Barbarian''" comes from the Greek "''βάρβαρος''" (''bárbaros''), meaning foreign. Dating back to the ancient Greek times, the Greeks referred to non-Greek people as barbarians because the language they spoke sounded to Greeks like gibberish represented by the sounds "''bar..bar..;''".
** In the Italian, Arabic, and Thai language settings of the game, the Elite Barbarians' name translates to "Chosen Barbarians", "Distinguished Barbarians", and "Skilled Barbarians" respectively.
** The Elite Barbarians are 1 of 6 [[cards]] associated with [[Barbarians]], with the others being [[Barbarian Launcher]], [[Battle Ram]], [[Barbarian Hut]], [[Barbarian Barrel]], and of course, Barbarians.
** According to a Clash-A-Rama comic [https://clasharama.fandom.com/wiki/Clash-A-Rama!_Comic_Strips?file=Barb_Barrel_ColourWeb2.jpg strip], the Barbarians follow a career path, with the Elite Barbarians being the highest-ranking ones.
* The Elite Barbarians are 1 of 7 troops that has had its movement speed classification changed, the others being [[Skeleton Barrel]], [[Suspicious Bush]], [[Goblin Cage|Goblin Brawler]], [[Cannon Cart]], [[Lumberjack]], and the [[Mighty Miner]].
* The Elite Barbarians are 1 of 23 troops that have been featured in the [[Troop Rush]] game [[:Category:Modes|mode]], the others being [[Skeletons]], [[Skeleton Dragons]], [[Fire Spirit]], [[Bats]], [[Firecracker]], [[Rascals|Rascal Girls]], [[Royal Hogs]], [[Heal Spirit]], [[Elixir Golem]], [[Guards]], [[Prince]], [[Balloon]], [[Golem]], [[Wall Breakers]], [[Ram Rider]], [[Sparky]], [[Phoenix]], [[Royal Ghost]], [[Bandit]], Lumberjack, [[Santa Hog Rider]], and the [[Monk]].
*The Elite Barbarians resemble the [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/Barbarian Level 6 Barbarian] in Clash of Clans. Their [[Star Points|Star Level 2 Skin]] resembles the Level 7 Barbarian in Clash of Clans.
*The helmets they wear may be a reference to the [[w:c:elderscrolls:Iron_Helmet_(Skyrim)|Iron Helmet]] that the [[w:c:elderscrolls:Last_Dragonborn|Dragonborn]] wears in the [[w:c:elderscrolls:The_Elder_Scrolls_V:_Skyrim|Elder Scrolls V: Skyrim]], which is one of the most iconic helmets in the game.
*In the card's description, the "''Harder, Better, Faster, Stronger''" line is a reference to the house song "''[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gAjR4_CbPpQ Harder, Better, Faster, Stronger]''" by the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daft_Punk Daft Punk].
*Elite Barbarians in [[Touchdown]] [[:Category:Modes|mode]] wear [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Football_helmet American football helmets] instead of their regular helmets seen in standard [[Basics of Battle|battle]].
*The Elite Barbarians are featured in non-Clash games. More specifically:
**The Elite Barbarians, along with the [[Archers]], [[Goblins]], Barbarians, and [[P.E.K.K.A.|P.E.K.K.A]], were featured as a [https://pad.fandom.com/wiki/Homepage/Monster monster] in [https://pad.fandom.com/wiki/Puzzle_%26_Dragons_Wiki Puzzles and Dragons], in a [https://pad.fandom.com/wiki/Homepage/Dungeon dungeon] called [https://pad.fandom.com/wiki/Clash_of_Clans_Dungeon Clash of Clans Dungeon].
***In Clash Royale, they are called "Elite Barbarians" but in Puzzles and Dragons, they are called "Rage Barbarians".
**While not available as a character, the Elite Barbarians are available as [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Barbarian?file=Barbarian_Classic_ability.png a promoted form for the Barbarian] in [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Squad_Busters_Wiki Squad Busters].
*The Elite Barbarians are the subject of 3 [[Emotes]].
**It is also 1 of 3 cards in which an Emote it is the subject of relates to one of its Star Levels, the others being the [[Hog Rider]] and [[Rocket]].

